      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">GST e-Way Bills are mandatory for transporting goods between states in India.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>These bills ensure smooth movement of goods across borders and help in facilitating the movement of goods without frequent checks.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>To comply with GST regulations, both the sender and receiver should generate and present GST e-Way Bills for the transportation from Faridabad to Mumbai.</span></li></ul>

	<p>In addition to GST e-Way Bills, IBA-approved Lorry Receipts (LR/Bilty) provide further evidence of the goods being transported. These documents serve as proof of the consignment details, including the sender, receiver, consignment number, and description of the goods. IBA LR/Bilty ensures secure transportation and reduces transit risks.</p>

